{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB11614 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "Rupatadine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Vasomotor Rhinitis through a chain of indications that connect it to Allergic Rhinitis and subsequently to Vasomotor Rhinitis. The evidence suggests that Rupatadine may act as a mediator in the development of Vasomotor Rhinitis, possibly by influencing allergic responses or inflammatory pathways. The shared indication of Allergic Rhinitis in all three paths points to a potential common mechanism, such as the modulation of histamine or other inflammatory mediators, which could contribute to the development of Vasomotor Rhinitis. The presence of distinct but related agents—Isoflupredone Acetate, Ramatroban, and Pheniramine—adds to the complexity, suggesting that Rupatadine may interact with different pathways that ultimately lead to Vasomotor Rhinitis. The integration of these indications highlights the role of Rupatadine in the broader context of allergic and inflammatory conditions, potentially supporting its repositioning for use in Vasomotor Rhinitis.",
